  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 228 PM EDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\n*** Friday through Mid Next Week ***\n\nA weak shortwave trough will bring chances for some rain showers on \nFriday, however confidence is low in timing or intensity at this \ntime. An upper level ridge will begin to build over the region at \nthe end of the week into the weekend. This will bring in a warmer \nand slightly drier air mass to the Ohio Valley. Maximum temperatures \nfor the weekend are expected to be in the mid to upper 90s, with \nheat indices potentially reaching triple digits. \n\nMoving into early next week, a frontal boundary is forecasted to \nmove through the area from the NW. This will bring rain chances back \ninto the forecast and possibly a brief relief in temperatures. \nHowever, this is not expected to last long as another warm airmass \nwill move back into for the middle of the week.",
